      "title": "Breaking News: Bihar Protest Row Deepens as Siwan Policeman Suspended, Opposition Targets Government in Parliament",
      "description": "<p data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"1\">The political controversy surrounding student protests in Bihar has intensified after a viral video from Siwan allegedly showed a police constable firing a rifle during demonstrations held amid the Bihar Bandh. The incident has sparked sharp political reactions, with opposition parties demanding accountability and raising the issue in Parliament. According to officials, the suspended personnel has been identified as SIT constable Abhishek Patel. Authorities have initiated an inquiry into the incident, while senior police officials have stated that a probe is underway to determine the circumstances surrounding the use of force during the protest. Opposition leader Tejashwi Yadav alleged that the constable fired at protesting students and questioned the deployment of such a weapon during crowd control. Reports also claimed that three students were injured during the unrest, though authorities have not officially confirmed whether the injuries were linked to the firing shown in the viral video. The controversy is expected to reverberate in Parliament, with opposition parties planning to press the government over police action against students and broader concerns regarding examination reforms. DMK MP T.R. Baalu has also submitted an adjournment motion seeking an urgent discussion on the NEET issue and demanding an investigation into the alleged use of lethal weapons during student demonstrations. The latest developments have added fresh political momentum to the ongoing debate over education reforms, student protests, and law enforcement practices. As investigations continue, both the Bihar administration and the Central Government are likely to face renewed scrutiny over the handling of protests and the measures taken to maintain public order.</p>",
